{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#120","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#120","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#120\",\"parent_revision\":\"d521b9cbdf849ee7c89e420551ac09c6a2ab4a69992458cc28a1ae8cf90758b6\",\"root_revision\":\"d521b9cbdf849ee7c89e420551ac09c6a2ab4a69992458cc28a1ae8cf90758b6\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`.pre-commit-config.yaml` pins `ruff-pre-commit` to its own version, unrelated to the `ruff` that `uv.lock` resolves. The two drift apart on every dependency bump, and the Prek hooks job then disagrees with the Code Linting job about which rules exist.\\n\\nPR #107 hit this concretely. Dependabot moved ruff `0.15.21 \u2192 0.16.3` in `uv.lock`; the hook stayed at `v0.15.6`. Every route to satisfying 0.16.3 broke the hook:\\n\\n- the `RUF201` fix writes rule *names* into the selector list, which 0.15.6 cannot parse\\n- the `RUF105` fix writes `# ruff: ignore[...]`, which 0.15.6 does not honour, resurfacing `BLE001`, `PLC0415`, and `F401`\\n\\nSo the pin had to move regardless of which fix was chosen. It was bumped to `v0.16.3` by hand to match.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nDerive the hook version from the lockfile, or have dependabot update both together, so a ruff bump cannot land with the hook disagreeing.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Related\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- #107 \u2014 where this surfaced\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"959e9fca5e27398106ed9084484d4b0648c1ab24bff22ba17ceb5524335b3970\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDORXxKvc8AAAABXP--eQ\"}"}